            "width": 92.73743016759778,
            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>Assassination and Aftermath</strong><br>\nSadat's presidency was cut short when he was assassinated on October 6, 1981, during a military parade. His death underscored the deep divisions within Egypt regarding his leadership and peace with Israel.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Sadat's Legacy</strong><br>\nSadat is remembered for his bold steps towards peace in the Middle East and his efforts to modernize Egypt. His legacy includes the controversial aftermath of the peace treaty, which still affects regional politics.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Remembering Anwar Sadat</strong><br>\nAnwar Sadat's impact on world history remains significant, as he is seen as a leader who dared to break from the past in pursuit of a vision for peace and development for Egypt and the broader region.</p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
                "license": "U",
                "title": "Unbenannt: Text",
